# Notes on reading the data

The Ask window gives these notes to Claude with every question, after the contract's views (docs/guides/ask.md).
Write what a careful reader of the views couldn't guess: units, signs, time zones, what to sum and what not to.
Keep them short: every line costs tokens on every question. (Examples: replace them with the app's own.)

- `v_daily.value` is the day's total. Sum it over days for a period total; never average the totals of periods
  of different lengths.
- A day is the local day ({{ timezone }}).
- A day with no row has no data: it is not a zero.
